{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>Also, you are slain by my sword</b> — like <i>turn back, all of you</i> and <i>come now</i>; it would have been fitting to say <i>all of you</i>, so too it would have been fitting to say <i>you are slain by my sword</i>. And Yefet said: like המ' [the demonstrative המה] with deficient kaf, and the meaning concerns Moab and Ammon who were mentioned."], :book :zephaniah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {0 "Resolved המ' as המה ('them/they') referenced as appearing with a deficient/missing kaf; alternatively could be an abbreviation, but the context of the grammatical argument about defective spelling supports reading it as the demonstrative pronoun המה cited in a deficient form."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Zephaniah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/zfanya"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:47:22.565455041Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}